        "title": "[rfc] OpenClaw Enterprise",
        "body": "Initial rfc out for OpenClaw Enterpries\r\n\r\nthis turned out to be more expansive in scope - found that laying out basic architecture also required adding implementation details for a bunch of platform drivers\r\nthe way to read this is a high level spec vs exact implementation details. lots to be fleshed out in impelmentations\r\n\r\nthe way to read this:\r\n- ./design.md: main design and overview of core entities\r\n    - ./iam.md: how access control works\r\n    - ./primitives.md: core entities in agent platform\r\n    - ./integrations.md: core drivers/adapters that will are responsible for realizing iam/primitives\r\n    - ./access-gateway.md: identity proxy that fronts our controller\r\n    - ./occ-console.md: admin/user routes and how they map on to integrations\r\n\r\nnote that instead of adding concrete interfaces, this spec is light on implementation but focuses on contracts of different components and how they compose in the platform. this also doesn't conform to our rfc format. will refactor this into a collection of different rfcs. just getting this out in pull request form now so we can review",
